  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Discovering Extracted Data**\n\nI\'ve got it! The extraction process has successfully produced complete JSON files. One, `/tmp/hki2022.json`, holds a 270-page book with 11 chapters, and the other, `/tmp/fkui_ed4.json`, is a behemoth at 1146 pages, spanning 56 chapters across 17 \"Seksi.\" Now, I\'m trying to recall the user\'s specific request.\n\n\n**Analyzing Current Files**\n\nI\'m now identifying the discrepancy: the `knowledge_books/` directory lacks the expected 35 markdown files. My current focus is reconciling this issue. I suspect that when the project was initialized or forked, the markdown files weren\'t present. The system is attempting to fill in placeholder texts with markdown file content. Thus I am currently focused on pinpointing the source of the markdown files that are required, so that I can fulfil the user\'s request.\n\n\n**Mapping Chapter Contents**\n\nI\'ve made progress! The PDFs, specifically `005._HKI_Buku_Ajar_Farmakologi_2022_4237e242.pdf` and `kupdf.net_farmakologi-dan-terapi-edisi-4_991d8e3d.pdf`, are accessible in `public/assets/aistudio/`. Now, the challenge is transforming these into chapter-level Markdown files. I\'ve confirmed we need 35 files: 11 for HKI 2022 (one per chapter), and 24 for FKUI Ed. 4 (grouping chapters by 17 Seksi or creating 24 files with major Bab). I\'m writing a script to map all 56 chapters of FKUI Ed. 4, as the PDF\'s chapter order isn\'t strictly sequential.\n\n\n**Validating Book Content**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the content to ensure accuracy and completeness. I\'m poring over the remaining pages of both HKI 2022 and FKUI Ed. 4 to cross-reference and validate all data points. This includes meticulously checking all facts slated for `labelHotspots.ts`, `kamusData.ts`, `panduanSimpanBuang.ts`, and `pustakaData.ts`. I\'m removing placeholder text and adding proper references where necessary in `pustakaData.ts`, and reviewing UI references as well. I\'m making sure we don\'t skip a single detail!\n\n\n"
