    thinking: "**Gathering Key Data**\n\nI\'ve just compiled authoritative facts from two sources: Buku Ajar Farmakologi (HKI, 2022), specifically chapters I through XI, and Farmakologi dan Terapi Edisi 4 (FKUI), focusing on chapters 1, 5, 15, 18, 33, 34, 38, and 39. This forms the foundational basis for my analysis.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Sources**\n\nI\'m now incorporating official Indonesian regulatory standards to enhance the data foundation. This includes leveraging information from BPOM RI, Kemenkes RI DAGUSIBU, Farmakope Indonesia Edisi VI, WHO, and USP. I\'m focusing on systematically updating placeholder data files and UI elements to integrate these references effectively, specifically targeting the replacement of placeholder titles and URLs with verified official titles and URLs in pustakaData.ts.\n\n\n**Integrating Reference Data**\n\nI\'m currently replacing placeholder content in several data files. Specifically, I am updating `labelHotspots.ts` and `kamusData.ts` with concise, accurate information sourced from HKI 2022, Farmakologi & Terapi Ed. 4, and Indonesian regulatory standards. Each entry is explicitly cited for clarity and accuracy. I also am integrating direct links within the Drug Question Assistant for all 35 sections of the HKI 2022 and Farmakologi & Terapi references.\n\n\n**Refining Regulatory Guidelines**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating specific regulatory guidelines. I\'m updating `simpanRules`, `buangRules`, and `catatanPenting` with clear, actionable guidance based on HKI 2022 (Bab VIII, IX, XI), Farmakologi & Terapi Ed. 4 (Bab 52), and DAGUSIBU guidelines. I\'m also removing placeholder text in `RujukanText.tsx` and updating references in `generatePdfClient.ts`, `DOKUMEN_PROTOTIPE_SKRIPSI.md`, and `LatihanPreviewView.tsx` with specific, grounded sources. Finally, I\'ve cleaned up placeholder URLs.\n\n\n"
